    An effective weight loss program combines four things: a sustainable calorie deficit, resistance training to protect muscle, adequate protein and daily movement, and a tracking and accountability system that keeps you consistent. Programs built on only one of these, usually severe food restriction, tend to be harder to maintain.
  </QuickAnswer>

